 "level_notes": {"0": "PUC-Lua (lua/lua mirror of the official sources) is the reference implementation; LuaJIT (trace JIT, Lua 5.1 + extensions) is the most important alternative. Official test suites are published at lua.org/tests.", "1": "The Lua Reference Manual (one per minor version, 5.4 is current stable and 5.5 the newest) is the definition; section anchors below point at the 5.4 manual. There is no formal standard; a PLT Redex mechanised semantics exists.", "2": "Programming in Lua (first edition, Lua 5.0) is freely online; later editions are paid books."},
